  "text_input": "Patient is a 74-year-old male, known case of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus for 10 years, presenting with cough with whitish mucoid expectoration for 5 days, acute onset shortness of breath (MMRC Grade 1 to 4) for 1 day, easy fatigability, and high-grade fever. Examination revealed tachycardia (106 bpm), SpO2 88% on room air, and bilateral crepitations in infra-scapular and infra-axillary areas. Investigations showed neutrophilic leukocytosis (WBC 19,310), HbA1c 12.2%, and chest X-ray/HRCT confirmed right lower lobe lobar pneumonia. 2D Echo showed LV diastolic dysfunction and EF 55%. USG showed hepatomegaly with fatty changes. Diagnosed with right lower lobe lobar pneumonia in sepsis with Type 1 respiratory failure and Type 2 DM with NPDR. Treated with antibiotics (Microtaz), insulin, and nebulization.",
